Source: unitpm
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Glyndor <packages@glyndor.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
# golang-go was here until the rewrite and nothing builds with Go any more.
# Cargo and rustc are deliberately not put in its place: debian/rules builds
# for a musl target and Debian's toolchain ships no musl standard library, so
# the compiler comes from the rustup toolchain the workflow pins to the same
# version rust-ci.yml uses. Naming Debian's rustc here would let
# dpkg-checkbuilddeps pass on a compiler that is not the one doing the work.
#
# The cost, so it reads as a decision: `dpkg-buildpackage` on a plain Debian
# box no longer works from Build-Depends alone, the musl target has to be
# installed first. Acceptable because this package is built by one workflow
# for one self-hosted archive, never submitted to the Debian archive.
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/Glyndor/unitpm
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/Glyndor/unitpm.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/Glyndor/unitpm
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: unitpm
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, adduser
Description: Secure, systemd-native process manager for Linux
 unitpm is a blazingly fast, modern, and secure process manager for Linux.
 It uses systemd as the supervisor engine and provides a CLI plus a
 user/system daemon for starting, stopping, scaling, and isolating
 applications (with optional DynamicUser or landlock sandboxing).
